{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldeans.</b> As a witness, for in the section of Lekh Lekha it was stated there, as I explained, and it was not stated in Haran." "And Abram trusted in HaShem, that his son would inherit it. And concerning the inheritance of the land he sought a sign, as Gideon did, and moreover, for the reason of HaShem's oath is that the matter be unconditional, for the principle of all prophecies is that they are conditional. And behold, Abram did not sin, because he sought to cut a covenant with Him:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:39.564173879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}